<title>AUSTRIA: SOCCER-ADMIRA WACKER PUNISHED FOR SUBSTITUTE MIX-UP.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-ADMIRA WACKER PUNISHED FOR SUBSTITUTE MIX-UP.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Admira Wacker had Saturday's 1-1</p>
<p>draw with Linz changed to a 3-0 defeat by the Austrian soccer</p>
<p>federation on Monday because they substituted too many players.</p>
<p>Admira coach Kurt Garger said he thought three outfield</p>
<p>players plus the goalkeeper could be replaced.</p>
<p>Austrian rules say only three changes can be made in a</p>
<p>league game although the infringement went unnoticed by referee</p>
<p>Stefan Messner.</p>
<p>Admira goalkeeper Franz Gruber was carried off after</p>
<p>suffering severe head injuries in a collision with Linz defender</p>
<p>Guenter Zeller.</p>
<p>Gruber underwent a five-hour operation on Sunday and will</p>
<p>miss the remainder of the season.</p>
